s9-4-p10 : Block
s9-4-p10 = prose (cons "The initial guard precedes every input read. Each shifted value is at most \(255\cdot256\), each completed field at most \(65535\), and the explicit unsigned-width conversions preserve those values. After the guard, \(n-4\) is defined; the second guard implies that the complete payload lies within the input. Failure leaves the output fields unchanged. Success writes exactly the tag, length, and borrowed payload view. These branch facts give the same source-level result as the interpreted decoder in §8.6, with output observations taken through the C fields rather than invented byte offsets." nil)
